  "key_findings": [
    "All 14 sessions fasted, Zone 1 dominant, zero anaerobic, perceived effort 1 of 5, recovery flag ready \u2014 100% repeatability confirming Gate 2 field implementability",
    "Metabolic flexibility progressed from Stable to Strong by Session 3 before any altitude or duration stress was introduced",
    "Cardiac Efficiency Index improved from 34.7 (Session 1) to 32.2 (Session 6) \u2014 lower cardiac cost per unit of distance across the Foundation phase",
    "Resting HR trend: 59 bpm (Session 1) to 53 bpm (Session 14) \u2014 progressive parasympathetic adaptation across the phase",
    "Sleep scores volatile (40-84 range) across Foundation phase \u2014 non-exercise stressors influence baseline architecture, not the sessions themselves",
    "Zero sleep quality degradation attributable to Foundation sessions \u2014 recovery flag remained ready regardless of sleep score",
    "Session 9 showed highest Zone 2 exposure (22%) and highest cardiac efficiency index (35.3) \u2014 slightly elevated thermal conditions (86F) modestly increased cardiac cost without disrupting the engine"
  ],
  "tg_differentiation": "Foundation is the proof of repeatability before complexity. Where the HWM dataset demonstrates what the system can do under extreme load, the Foundation dataset demonstrates that the system was built deliberately \u2014 14 fasted, low-intensity sessions on flat terrain establishing aerobic calm, metabolic substrate flexibility, and recovery readiness before a single alpine hike was attempted. The progression from Stable to Strong metabolic flexibility within the Foundation phase alone confirms that substrate discipline is trainable at the entry level, independent of altitude or duration stress.",
